'' A UDT WHOSE CONST IS ADDED IS ONE TIER DOWN, as fbc scores any same-type match whose
'' CONST differs: below EVERY derived-to-base conversion, above 'any ptr'. tiko-lang costed
'' adding const one step above exact, so a T2 offered { byref const T2, byref T1 } ran the
'' const T2 body where fbc-modern runs T1 (measured 2026-09-19) -- and the same for a T3
'' two links down, a T2 offered { const T1, T1 } (which tiko had TIED and ran the head of,
'' silently), a 'T2 ptr' offered { const T2 ptr, T1 ptr }, and byval. Adding const to a
'' base ranks by distance, so { const T2, const T1 } still takes const T2 (f4), and
'' { const T2 ptr, any ptr } still takes the const pointer (f6).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/overload-const-udt.bas
